From 9c446b3bf268c6f4612ba7f03b278d523e3bb080 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raxcoms <mpaulo968@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:00:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] gamescope: add Auto HDR presentation

Add opt-in AutoHDR for SDR games using a separate shaper/3D-LUT pair.
Reuse Gamescope's SDR gamut mapping, LUT builder, gain, white balance,
output encoding and Vulkan sampling, plus Armada's existing DRM plane
color pipelines. The new BT.2446 A stage runs during LUT generation and
scales RGB together toward the display peak.

Tag only the held SDR game's base layer. Require HDR support and an
unleased LUT plane on the primary CRTC; exclude lease clients, legacy
ITM and override LUTs. Constrain liftoff to a compatible plane and leave
SDR overlays on their normal tables. Composition samples the same game
LUTs when already required. No forced-composition condition is added;
failed plane allocation still uses Gamescope's normal fallback.

Track LUT changes and clear stale bindings in reused frames, partial
composites and captures. Report converted HDR to Steam only after a
successful primary presentation. Keep the existing SDR/native HDR LUTs.

Update-sensitive points are LUT-builder stage order, shared C++/GLSL LUT
slots, base-layer identity in upscalers/partial composites, and DRM plane
allocation/colorop APIs. Review those changes and retest scanout, overlays
and leases even if the patch applies. The numerical tests cover the curve
and LUT output, not presentation behavior.
